            "[Source: faq_warranties.md]\n---\n\n### Q7.3: What does the Total Protection (Accidental Damage) Plan cover?\n\n**Answer:**\nThe **Total Protection Plan** covers:\n\n✅ **Covered:**\n- Manufacturing defects\n- Internal component failures\n- Accidental drops — cracked screens, internal damage\n- Liquid damage from spills\n- Electrical surge damage (not floods)\n- Charging port and button failures\n\n❌ **Not covered:**\n- Theft or loss\n- Cosmetic damage without functional impact (minor scratches)\n- Damage due to intentional acts\n- War, natural disasters, flooding\n- Pre-existing conditions (damage present before plan purchase)\n\n**Claim limits:** Most plans allow up to **2 accidental damage claims** per year. Check your specific plan terms.",
            "### Q7.4: How do I make a claim under an extended warranty plan?\n\n**Answer:**\nClaiming under our extended warranty plan is straightforward:",
            "[Source: faq_warranties.md]\n---\n\n### Q2.2: What is NOT covered by a manufacturer's warranty?\n\n**Answer:**\nThe following are typically **excluded** from manufacturer warranties:\n\n- **Physical damage** — cracks, dents, broken screens from drops or impacts\n- **Water damage** — unless the product is rated waterproof and the damage was within rated limits\n- **Electrical damage** — from power surges, incorrect voltage, or improper use\n- **Damage from unauthorized repairs** — repairs done outside authorized service centers\n- **Cosmetic damage** — scratches, dents that don't affect functionality\n- **Consumables** — batteries (after capacity degrades normally), printer ink/toner, filters\n- **Normal wear and tear** — gradual degradation from regular use\n- **Pest damage** — rodent chewing, insect damage\n- **Loss or theft** — warranties don't cover missing products\n- **Improper installation** — damage caused by incorrect setup\n- **Software issues** — viruses, malware, software conflicts (in most cases)",
