            "### Q8.2: What warranty applies to home appliances (refrigerators, ACs, washing machines)?\n\n**Answer:**\nHome appliances typically have layered warranties:",
            "[Source: faq_warranties.md]\n- **Unauthorized repairs or modifications** — opening the device yourself or using a non-authorized repair shop\n- **Removing or altering the serial number** — this is often illegal and always voids the warranty\n- **Tampering with seals or stickers** — many devices have tamper-evident stickers inside or on screws\n- **Rooting or jailbreaking** (for phones/tablets) — software modification may void warranty on some brands\n- **Using third-party accessories that cause damage** — e.g., a non-certified charger that damages the battery\n- **Physical damage** — the manufacturer may void the entire warranty if the device shows physical damage, arguing the damage may have caused the defect\n- **Improper installation or use** — using the product in conditions or for purposes outside its specifications (e.g., using a non-outdoor appliance outdoors)\n- **Damage caused by pests, floods, fire, or acts of nature** — unless covered by a specific protection plan",
